## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the candidate's understanding of end-to-end testing for real-time, distributed systems with regional routing, data consistency, and feature flag safety.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing of event-driven pipelines, cross-region latency, and eventual consistency
- Test data isolation and deterministic environments via mocks and seed data
- Idempotency, replay safety, and rollback semantics for feature flags
- Instrumentation hooks to seed Kafka, mock external feeds, and reset Redis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright test scaffold for the trading alert pipeline
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test.describe('Multi-Region Alerting System', () => {
  let kafkaSeeder;
  let redisClient;
  let mockExternalFeed;

  test.beforeEach(async () => {
    // Seed isolated test data per region
    await redisClient.flushdb();
    await kafkaSeeder.seedEvents([
      { region: 'us-east', symbol: 'AAPL', threshold: 150 },
      { region: 'eu-west', symbol: 'BMW', threshold: 85 },
    ]);
    mockExternalFeed.setDeterministicResponse({ AAPL: { price: 152 }, BMW: { price: 87 } });
  });

  test('alerts propagate to correct regional dashboards', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('https://dashboard.trading.example.com');
    await expect(page.locator('.alert').first()).toBeVisible({ timeout: 5000 });

    // Verify cross-region routing
    const alerts = await page.locator('.alert').all();
    expect(alerts).toHaveLength(2);
  });

  test('feature flag rollback triggers correctly', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('https://dashboard.trading.example.com');
    await page.evaluate(() => window.triggerRollback());
    await expect(page.locator('.rollback-success')).toBeVisible();
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests for feature flags are essential to validate UI gating, state persistence, and how flows handle mid-flight flag changes in real user journeys.

## Key Concepts
- Feature flags and gating
- Test data seeding and API-driven state setup
- End-to-end verification of UI state and backend persistence
- Handling mid-flow toggling and UI consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('onboarding with feature flag', async ({ page, request }) => {
  // Seed user with onboarding flag ON
  await request.post('/api/test/setup-user', { data: { flagName: 'new-onboarding', value: true } });
  // Login and navigate
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.fill('#email', 'user@example.com');
  await page.fill('#password', 's3cret');
  await page.click('button[type="submit"]');
  await page.waitForURL('/dashboard');

  // Verify onboarding visible
  await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-panel')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-panel .step')).toHaveCount(4);

  // Complete first step
  await page.click('#step-1 .complete');
  await expect(page.locator('#step-1')).toHaveClass(/completed/);

  // Refresh and verify persistence
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#step-1')).toHaveClass(/completed/);

  // Turn flag OFF mid-flow and verify UI hides, but backend progress remains
  await request.post('/api/test/setup-user', { data: { flagName: 'new-onboarding', value: false } });
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#onboarding-panel')).toBeHidden();

  // Validate backend progress still retrievable
  const res = await request.get('/api/user/progress');
  expect(res.status()).toBe(200);
  const data = await res.json();
  expect(data.stepsCompleted).toBe(1);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
